Package: adaptiveFFT
Title: Adaptive Fast-and-Frugal Trees with Inner-Holdout Family Selection
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(person(given = "Travis", family = "Jakel",
             email = "travis.s.jakel@gmail.com",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(affiliation = "Asset Flow Capital")),
      person(given = "Asset Flow Capital", role = "cph"))
Description: Chain Fast-and-Frugal Trees (FFTs) of depth at most four, with
    one cue per node and binary exits, fit by either the FFTrees greedy
    'ifan' algorithm or by a beam search over the chain space whose
    hyperparameters were selected via D-optimal Design of Experiments.
    The 'adaptive_fft()' constructor performs an inner-holdout race
    between the two families and refits the winner on the full training
    set. Includes the 14-dataset benchmark harness (FFTrees-bundled
    datasets) used in Jakel (2026) showing a +1.4 pp balanced-accuracy
    point estimate over 'ifan' across 14 datasets x 20 stratified seeds
    while preserving strict chain-FFT structure.
